Mechanism and files
src/capability.rs:21,57,73,99 — shared typed consumer, adapted with origin credit
from bboxy450-term. Pre-open metadata rejects symlinks and non-regular files;
O_NOFOLLOW|O_NONBLOCK open is followed by descriptor fstat, regular-file/euid/
exact 0600 checks. Bounded reading accepts exactly 64 lowercase hex plus newline.
The returned value and temporary buffer use Zeroizing. Refusal text consists
only of fixed seat_admission_file_* codes, without path/value/OS error text.
File IO runs through runtime::blocking. Reading preserves the overlay file.

src/redact.rs:45-76 — each face's shared Set captures initialization, the
validated admission value and a safe refusal. The value is registered before
provider, tool or MCP startup; the MCP check uses this captured value rather
than consulting the removed raw environment variable.

src/frontends/headless.rs:132 — bootstrap precedes closed replay and provider
creation; seat and ACP use this same entry. Closed replay is scrubbed too.
src/frontends/gui/bridge.rs:117,157,424 — replay and live GUI creation register
on workers before transcript projection or Host/provider/MCP startup.
src/frontends/gui/smoke.rs:18 — offscreen replay registers before parsing and
rendering. GUI FrameState/view status exposes a safe degradation Notice.
src/frontends/smoke.rs:35 — optional live-smoke face registers even before its
no-provider-key skip. src/engine/mod.rs:235 persists a safe startup Notice for
missing/invalid input, without aborting the session.

src/mcp.rs:578-581 — profile/ACP resolved environment values are refused when
they contain the captured capability. Existing reserved-reference/config-key
checks remain. The immutable Launcher origin retains its ICD §5 exception:
--mcp-config servers inherit/reference BBOXY_* including the file path. This is
intentional; profile/ACP servers and their command resolvers do not inherit it.
src/process.rs:477 — tools, terminals and command resolvers unconditionally
remove every inherited BBOXY_* name, including BBOXY_CAPABILITY_FILE.

Test fixtures now create their own private 0600 files instead of supplying the
legacy value in env. scripts/test.py, tests/gui_gate.py and the GUI control
runner remove the real seat's file path in their private test environments.
No production BBOXY_CAPABILITY setter or compatibility fallback was added.
Changes are inside src/, tests/, scripts/, verification/ and .bboxy/runs/.
No new dependency, core policy change, merge, publication or installation.

ICD verification cases and real-process witnesses
tests/capability_delivery.rs:292,298,305 — real headless, seat and ACP binaries
start with only a private capability file. Their actual shell tool executes
printenv, cat "$BBOXY_CAPABILITY_FILE", printenv BBOXY_CAPABILITY_FILE, then cat
with an explicit literal path. The env/path probes reveal no BBOXY_* entries
and no value. The explicit-path output is exactly <redacted>. Assertions inspect
completed ToolCall output, stdout/stderr, transcript laws and every actual
session file/blob, not a mocked scrubber. The original file remains unchanged.
This covers ICD cases (a) and (b), and the requested output-redaction witness.

tests/support/seat_launch.rs:11,493,509 — production launcher/profile/ACP MCP
processes witness the origin-specific environment rules. Profile/ACP echo_env
reports no reserved namespace or admission value; launcher echo_env confirms
its file path is present and the legacy value is absent. Case (c).
tests/capability_delivery.rs:390 — real profile and ACP !cmd resolvers read the
private file through a literal path. A resolved value equal to the admission
value is refused before its MCP server starts (no report file); a safe Notice
is emitted and the user turn completes. Case (d), resolved-value comparison.

tests/capability_delivery.rs:311 — missing path, symlink, wrong mode, malformed
content, directory and absent environment all produce fixed Notices and still
complete a turn. Notices contain neither the rejected path nor file content.
src/capability.rs:127,173 — three unit witnesses cover canonical bounded reads,
file preservation, invalid size/newline/case, symlink/type/mode and foreign uid
metadata refusal before reading. No foreign secret is read.
tests/capability_delivery.rs:368 — optional live-smoke startup checks its file
and emits WrongMode before its isolated no-key skip.
tests/capability_delivery.rs:431 — two actual offscreen GUI subprocesses render
otherwise identical fixtures: one embeds the private value, the other embeds
<redacted>. PNG bytes are equal; stdout/stderr contain no value. This checks
GUI smoke loading before projection/rendering, rather than only a helper call.

